  "question": {
    "text": "If the function <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>A</mi></math> defined as <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math> is a surjective function, then the set <math><mi>A</mi></math> is&nbsp;"
  },
